# Alt+Tab Foreground Sync and Feature Hotkey Latch (Mandatory — Do Not Regress)

**Status:** Verified working on Windows (2026-07-24, v0.8.293–v0.8.294; foreground path rewritten v0.8.330). User-confirmed: Alt+Tab away and back to linked main target must **not** leave feature hotkeys dead until PIPBONG is focused once.

## Symptom

Main target focused → hotkeys work → Alt+Tab away → Alt+Tab back → hotkeys dead → focus PIPBONG once → hotkeys work again.

**Not** the same as user-held Shift release ([physical-keyboard-preservation.mdc](./physical-keyboard-preservation.mdc)).

## Root cause (two layers)

| Layer | Detail |
| ----- | ------ |
| Foreground sync (v0.8.293, v0.8.330) | `ForegroundWindowMonitor` must deliver `foregroundChanged` on GUI thread; empty-caption games need process-path profile/capture match; `FeatureHotkeyGate` must **not** block `applyProfileSwitchFromForegroundState` |
| Hook latch (v0.8.294) | Missed KEYUP / mouse UP during Alt+Tab → toggle `armed=false` or mouse `buttonDown=true` → hook swallows next hotkey without firing |

## Required architecture

| API | Role |
| --- | ---- |
| `ForegroundWindowMonitor` | Sole WinEvent `EVENT_SYSTEM_FOREGROUND` detector; `foregroundChanged` + `altModifierReleased`; `currentState()` for gates — **no** MainWindow poll timer |
| `onForegroundStateChanged` | Profile switch via `applyProfileSwitchFromForegroundState`; capture adopt; `maybeResetHotkeyLatchForForeground`; `finishForegroundSessionGate` |
| `onForegroundAltModifierReleased` | `flushDeferredProfileSwitchIfIdle` + `resetHookLatchState` |
| `HotkeyManager::resetHookLatchState` | `hold keyDown=false`, `toggle armed=true`, `mouse buttonDown=false`; **no** `hotkeyHoldEnded` emit |
| `maybeResetHotkeyLatchForForeground` | Once per linked-target foreground HWND (`m_lastHotkeyLatchResetForegroundHwnd`) |
| `ensureForegroundReadyForFeatureHotkey` | From `onHotkeyTriggered` / `onHotkeyHoldStarted`: capture adopt/sync + latch reset — **no** redundant foreground poll |

## Anti-patterns

- Capture/profile sync only (v0.8.289–0.8.292) — insufficient for latch stuck state
- Reintroduce 100 ms `QTimer` foreground poll or scattered `GetForegroundWindow` in `MainWindow.cpp`
- `resetHookLatchState` on every foreground tick — breaks hold mode
- Emit hold-ended from latch reset
- Require PIPBONG focus to heal hotkeys after Alt+Tab

## Manual verify

Alt+Tab away/back **without** focusing PIPBONG; keyboard toggle + mouse side-button bindings; repeat 5×.

